{"kind":"send","message":{"emittedAtMs":1792508085100,"method":"turn/moderationMetadata","params":{"metadata":{"generation":{},"prompt":{"omnimod":{"outputs":[{"is_blocked":false,"results":[{"category_flags":{"A1":false,"A2":false,"A3":false,"C1":false,"C11":false,"C2":false,"CBRN-B1+":false,"E1":false,"E2":false,"E3":false,"H1":false,"H2":false,"H3":false,"IMG-C1":false,"IMG-C11":false,"IMG-C2":false,"IMG-S1":false,"IMG-SH":false,"IMG-V1":false,"IMG-V2+":false,"IMG-V4+":false,"JB1":false,"K1":false,"K2":false,"K3":false,"K4":false,"P1":false,"P2":false,"P3":false,"P4":false,"PD1":false,"PD4":false,"REFUSED":false,"S1":false,"S3+":false,"S4":false,"SH":false,"TXT-C3":false,"TXT-C4":false,"V1":false,"V2+":false,"V4+":false}}]}],"protection_type":"omnimod"}},"tool_call":{},"tool_response":{}},"threadId":"01a159ce-a3e7-7653-8390-a50314e2d2bb","turnId":"01a159ce-a70d-7461-9ffa-beb568646d81"}}}
{"kind":"send","message":{"emittedAtMs":1792508085105,"method":"item/completed","params":{"completedAtMs":1792508085100,"item":{"delivery":null,"id":"msg_005e0935a36e8052016ad780b344f08191879f1eebba3ec0a8","memoryCitation":null,"phase":"final_answer","questions":null,"text":"`if (!items.length \u0026\u0026 isEnabled)` is true only when both conditions are true:\n\n1. `items.length` is `0`, so `!items.length` becomes `true`.\n2. `isEnabled` is truthy—normally `true`.\n\nIt is false if the array has any elements or if `isEnabled` is false.\n\n| `items` | `items.length` | `!items.length` | `isEnabled` | Overall result |\n|---|---:|---:|---|---|\n| `[]` | `0` | `true` | `true` | `true` |\n| `[]` | `0` | `true` | `false` | `false` |\n| `[1]` | `1` | `false` | `true` | `false` |\n| `[1]` | `1` | `false` | `false` | `false` |\n\nPotential pitfalls:\n\n- `!items.length` relies on numeric truthiness: `0` is falsy, positive numbers are truthy.\n- If `items` is `null` or `undefined`, accessing `.length` throws an error.\n- It can be less obvious to readers than explicitly checking for zero.\n- It assumes `items` has a meaningful numeric `length`, not merely that it is an array.\n\nComparison:\n\n```js\nif (items.length === 0 \u0026\u0026 isEnabled)\n```\n\nThis has the same behavior for a normal array, but is clearer and more explicit. It still throws if `items` is nullish.\n\n```js\nif (!items?.length \u0026\u0026 isEnabled)\n```\n\nThis avoids an exception when `items` is `null` or `undefined`. However, it treats a missing `items` value as empty, because `items?.length` produces `undefined`, and `!undefined` is `true`.\n\nFor production code, use:\n\n```js\nif (items.length === 0 \u0026\u0026 isEnabled)\n```\n\nwhen `items` is guaranteed to be an array. It is the clearest and safest version because it states the intended condition directly. Use the optional-chaining version only when `null` or `undefined` genuinely should mean “no items”; otherwise, validate or initialize `items` first.","type":"agentMessage"},"threadId":"01a159ce-a3e7-7653-8390-a50314e2d2bb","turnId":"01a159ce-a70d-7461-9ffa-beb568646d81"}}}
